run-kde: what the guest needs, and what this machine has
  ✓ this is WSL 2 (5.15.167.4-microsoft-standard-WSL2)
  ✓ nix is installed
  ✗ KVM: @T@/absent does not exist, and the guest needs it
      the CPU's virtualization flags (svm or vmx) are not visible here, so nested virtualization is off
      in %UserProfile%\.wslconfig, under [wsl2], set: nestedVirtualization=true
      and turn on SVM (AMD) or VT-x (Intel) in the firmware setup of the machine
  ✓ FUSE: @T@/fuse can be opened
  ✓ virtiofsd: starts as this user and serves a directory
  ! memory: this machine has 6144 MB, so the guest gets 4096 MB (8192 is comfortable)
      in %UserProfile%\.wslconfig, under [wsl2], set: memory=12GB
  ✓ cores: this machine has 12, and the guest gets 6
  ✓ disk: 100 GB are free for the Nix store (@T@)
  ✓ a window can be shown (WAYLAND_DISPLAY=w)
  ! Windows interop: mstsc.exe or cmdkey.exe cannot be run, which --rdp needs
      on NixOS-WSL, wsl.interop.includePath = true; (and wsl.interop.register = true;)
  ! GPU: there is no @T@/absent, so the guest renders on its CPUs
      install the Windows GPU driver with WSL support; on NixOS-WSL, wsl.useWindowsDriver = true;
  ✓ the guest will not use the GPU: there is no @T@/absent, so WSL has no GPU
